{
	"id": "sveltekit-og",
	"name": "SvelteKit OG",
	"repo": "ethercorps/sveltekit-og",
	"url": "https://github.com/ethercorps/sveltekit-og",
	"summary": "A SvelteKit library that makes Open Graph images from HTML/CSS or a Svelte component without a browser: version 4 from main, and the 5.0.0-next pre-release from the v5 branch, side by side.",
	"description": "Each version's public API and render pipeline, in packages v4 and v5, so the same names (ImageResponse, BaseFont, render) can be compared: v4 has a class and a render path per engine; v5 one shared ImageResponse and one pipeline, Takumi by default. Notes on the v5 diagrams say what changed.",
	"notes": "v4: Intersection option types (ImageOptions & ResponseImageOptions, TakumiImageOptions & TakumiResponseOptions) are drawn as one interface generalizing the image half, with the response fields folded in; ClientImageResponseOptions is a TS union, drawn as an interface with dependencies to its two alternatives. TS unions were narrowed to the main type (element: string, output: Uint8Array, font bytes: ArrayBuffer); TakumiImageOptions.fonts also accepts TakumiFontDescriptor (not drawn). Left out to stay under 14: client engines and client createImage, the sveltekitOG Vite plugin, and the emoji, defaults and error-handler helpers. v5: No Engine interface exists: Engine is the union \"takumi\" | \"satori\" (an attribute type here, not drawn), the two engine modules share render(vnode, options) only by convention, serverPlatform/clientPlatform are const objects drawn as classes realizing Platform, and the stub is source text from plugin.stubSource, not a class. ResponseOptions is folded into ImageResponseOptions; unions narrowed (render results drawn Promise<Uint8Array>, svg actually yields a string; Satori format string = png or svg; FontInput also admits FontDescriptor). Left out for the 14 limit: core/packages.ts (installMessage), helpers/response.ts, the memoized providers and client wasm/font loaders, FONT_CACHE_MAP, resolveFonts, ErrorCodes.",
